1
00:00:00,433 --> 00:00:02,467
Are you a SMART fella...

2
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,533
or a FART smella?

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,800
Let's find OUT!

4
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:10,467
Question three, a picture puzzle!

5
00:00:10,467 --> 00:00:12,967
An empty circle becomes a filled-in

6
00:00:12,967 --> 00:00:16,000
circle. So an empty square becomes...

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,467
which one? A,

8
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:18,867
a filled square...

9
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:21,200
B, an empty square...

10
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,067
C, a filled circle...

11
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:25,500
or D, a filled triangle?

12
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,967
Five seconds!

13
00:00:32,467 --> 00:00:35,000
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

14
00:00:35,367 --> 00:00:36,767
The answer is...

15
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:39,000
A, a filled square!

16
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,567
The rule is simple:

17
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:42,167
the shape gets colored in,

18
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:44,533
but stays the very same shape.

19
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:47,867
Empty square becomes filled square!

20
00:00:48,733 --> 00:00:51,467
Question six, a word analogy!

21
00:00:51,467 --> 00:00:52,867
Ocean is to puddle,

22
00:00:52,867 --> 00:00:54,767
as mountain is to...

23
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:57,200
what? A, valley...

24
00:00:57,367 --> 00:00:59,600
B, hill... C,

25
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,233
river... or D,

26
00:01:01,233 --> 00:01:03,467
rock? Five seconds!

27
00:01:08,967 --> 00:01:11,500
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

28
00:01:11,867 --> 00:01:14,500
It's... B, hill!

29
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,333
An ocean shrinks down to a

30
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:18,667
tiny puddle, so a mountain shrinks

31
00:01:18,667 --> 00:01:20,400
down to a little hill.

32
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,900
Same thing, pocket-sized!

33
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:26,633
Question nine, a number series!

34
00:01:26,633 --> 00:01:28,667
One, one, two,

35
00:01:28,667 --> 00:01:30,667
three, five, eight,

36
00:01:30,667 --> 00:01:33,133
and then... what comes next?

37
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:35,133
A, eleven... B,

38
00:01:35,133 --> 00:01:37,667
thirteen... C, twelve...

39
00:01:37,667 --> 00:01:39,800
or D, sixteen?

40
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,233
Five seconds!

41
00:01:46,733 --> 00:01:49,267
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

42
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,133
The answer is...

43
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:53,800
B, thirteen! Add the two numbers

44
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:56,000
before it: five plus eight is

45
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,633
thirteen. That's the famous Fibonacci pattern!

46
00:02:00,467 --> 00:02:03,467
Question thirteen, a picture puzzle!

47
00:02:03,467 --> 00:02:05,733
A dot marches clockwise around

48
00:02:05,733 --> 00:02:07,600
a square: top-left,

49
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,833
top-right, bottom-right... where

50
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:11,500
does it jump next?

51
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,933
A, top-left... B,

52
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:16,867
bottom-left... C, top-right...

53
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:18,700
or D, the center?

54
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,467
Five seconds!

55
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,533
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

56
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:30,200
The answer is...

57
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,733
B, bottom-left! The dot steps clockwise,

58
00:02:33,733 --> 00:02:34,800
corner to corner,

59
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,467
and right after bottom-right,

60
00:02:36,467 --> 00:02:38,867
the next corner is bottom-left!

61
00:02:39,867 --> 00:02:42,333
Question ten! Which one does NOT

62
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:45,333
belong? Add... subtract...

63
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:48,300
multiply... number. A,

64
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:51,100
add... B, subtract...

65
00:02:51,367 --> 00:02:54,100
C, multiply... or D,

66
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:56,733
number? Five seconds!

67
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,933
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

68
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:07,833
It's... D, number!

69
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:10,500
Add, subtract, and multiply are

70
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:11,800
all things you do.

71
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:12,767
But a number?

72
00:03:12,767 --> 00:03:15,067
That's the thing you do them to!

73
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:18,467
Question seven, and this one is

74
00:03:18,467 --> 00:03:21,167
tricky! Two, six,

75
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:24,000
twelve, twenty, thirty,

76
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,967
and then... what comes next?

77
00:03:27,067 --> 00:03:29,733
A, thirty-six... B,

78
00:03:29,733 --> 00:03:32,933
forty... C, forty-two...

79
00:03:32,933 --> 00:03:35,300
or D, forty-four?

80
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,133
Five seconds on the clock!

81
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,333
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

82
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:47,033
The answer is...

83
00:03:47,033 --> 00:03:50,000
C, forty-two! Look at the jumps:

84
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
plus four, plus six,

85
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
plus eight, plus ten.

86
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,167
The next jump is plus twelve,

87
00:03:56,167 --> 00:03:59,300
and thirty plus twelve is forty-two!

88
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:03,000
Question eleven, a shape puzzle!

89
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,167
Watch them grow,

90
00:04:04,167 --> 00:04:06,433
gaining one side each step:

91
00:04:06,433 --> 00:04:08,533
a triangle, then a square,

92
00:04:08,533 --> 00:04:09,933
then a pentagon.

93
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:11,733
Which shape comes next?

94
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:13,133
A, a circle...

95
00:04:13,133 --> 00:04:15,267
B, a hexagon...

96
00:04:15,333 --> 00:04:16,700
C, a square...

97
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,900
or D, an octagon?

98
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:20,467
Five seconds!

99
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,533
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

100
00:04:28,867 --> 00:04:30,333
The answer is...

101
00:04:30,333 --> 00:04:33,333
B, hexagon! Count the sides:

102
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:35,933
triangle three, square four,

103
00:04:35,933 --> 00:04:38,633
pentagon five... so next up is

104
00:04:38,633 --> 00:04:41,167
the six-sided hexagon!

105
00:04:42,067 --> 00:04:45,033
Question fourteen, a number analogy!

106
00:04:45,033 --> 00:04:46,167
Two makes five,

107
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:47,367
three makes seven,

108
00:04:47,367 --> 00:04:48,633
four makes nine,

109
00:04:48,633 --> 00:04:50,167
so five makes...

110
00:04:50,167 --> 00:04:52,000
what? A, ten...

111
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,967
B, eleven... C,

112
00:04:53,967 --> 00:04:55,600
twelve... or D,

113
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,967
thirteen? Five seconds!

114
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:06,000
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

115
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:08,833
It's... B, eleven!

116
00:05:08,833 --> 00:05:10,300
Each number is doubled,

117
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:11,733
then add one.

118
00:05:11,733 --> 00:05:13,733
Five times two is ten,

119
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:16,033
plus one is eleven!

120
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:19,567
Question twelve, fill in the blank!

121
00:05:19,567 --> 00:05:21,233
The bridge was too weak to

122
00:05:21,233 --> 00:05:22,467
hold the heavy truck,

123
00:05:22,467 --> 00:05:24,367
so workers had to blank it

124
00:05:24,367 --> 00:05:25,933
before opening the road.

125
00:05:25,933 --> 00:05:28,167
A, decorate... B,

126
00:05:28,167 --> 00:05:30,933
reinforce... C, rename...

127
00:05:30,933 --> 00:05:32,567
or D, measure?

128
00:05:32,567 --> 00:05:33,900
Five seconds!

129
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,933
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

130
00:05:42,333 --> 00:05:45,100
It's... B, reinforce!

131
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:46,700
Too weak means you have to

132
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:47,833
make it stronger,

133
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:50,133
and reinforce is the only word

134
00:05:50,133 --> 00:05:51,933
that fixes the problem!

135
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,267
Last one, question fifteen,

136
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:56,700
a number puzzle,

137
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:58,133
and it's sneaky!

138
00:05:58,133 --> 00:06:00,533
If four plus five makes twenty,

139
00:06:00,533 --> 00:06:02,833
three plus six makes eighteen,

140
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:05,633
and two plus seven makes fourteen...

141
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:08,433
then five plus four makes...

142
00:06:08,433 --> 00:06:10,833
what? A, nine...

143
00:06:10,867 --> 00:06:13,167
B, eighteen... C,

144
00:06:13,167 --> 00:06:14,767
twenty... or D,

145
00:06:14,767 --> 00:06:17,200
twenty-five? Five seconds!

146
00:06:22,667 --> 00:06:25,200
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

147
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:26,967
The answer is...

148
00:06:26,967 --> 00:06:29,400
C, twenty! Here's the trick:

149
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:32,700
that plus sign secretly means multiply.

150
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:34,500
Four times five is twenty,

151
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:37,600
so five times four is twenty too!

152
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:41,567
So, are you smart or fart?

153
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:43,333
Count up your correct answers to

154
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:44,967
find your rank!

155
00:06:45,833 --> 00:06:47,433
So, how did you do?

156
00:06:47,433 --> 00:06:48,933
Comment your score below,

157
00:06:48,933 --> 00:06:50,767
and subscribe for more!
